---
import type { ProfileMeta, ProfileSection } from "../../lib/profile";
import Cards from "../../components/Cards.astro";
import GalleryCard from "../../components/GalleryCard.astro";
import InfoCard from "../../components/InfoCard.astro";
import LogbookCard from "../../components/LogbookCard.astro";
import Prose from "../../components/Prose.astro";
import SectionBlock from "../../components/SectionBlock.astro";
import SectionCluster from "../../components/SectionCluster.astro";

export const profile: ProfileMeta = {
  lang: "en",
  stationId: "BD4WXB",
  callsign: "BD4WXB",
  status: "inactive",
  pageTitle: "chariri's Personal Amateur Radio Station",
  description:
    "Station information, QSL policy, and gallery for the personal amateur radio station BD4WXB.",
  hero: {
    quote: '<span lang="ja">忘れたくない想い、ありますか？</span>',
    quoteSource: "ef - a tale of memories.",
  },
};

export const sections: readonly ProfileSection[] = [
  { id: "basic-info", label: "Basic Info" },
  { id: "showcase", label: "Showcase" },
  { id: "logbook", label: "Logbook" },
];
---

<Prose>
  <p>
    Welcome to the homepage of my personal amateur radio station. You are also welcome to visit
    <a href="https://chariri.moe/">my blog</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Since I have left Nanjing, the callsign BD4WXB has been inactive since September 3, 2025. You
    can use the links at the top of this page to switch to the callsign I currently use: JL1HRE.
  </p>
  <p>
    As you can see, this page vibecoded. This was my first vibecoding project, and it ended up
    taking 26 hours -- far longer than I expected. My feeling is that AI often produces code that
    lacks taste. With high-performance LLM models, it’s easy to vibecode 'usable' front-end code.
    But it’s difficult to generate code that’s elegant, comprehensive (for example, you’ll notice
    this page has I18n, A11y, printing, and dark mode support), and visually appealing. Yet, it's
    still far easier than writing from scratch.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of my longer notes and murmuring about amateur radio are on my blog. <a
      href="https://chariri.moe/archives/1957/amateur-radio/"
    >
      The link is here.
    </a>
  </p>
</Prose>

<SectionBlock id="basic-info" title="Basic Info">
  <Cards columns="2u">
    <InfoCard label="QTH" icon="grid">
      OL39
      <Fragment slot="description">CRAC Area 8 - Chongqing</Fragment>
    </InfoCard>
    <InfoCard label="License" icon="signal">
      China Amateur Radio Class B Operator License + Class B Station License
      <Fragment slot="description">
        144 MHz @ 25 W<br />
        HF @ 15 W
      </Fragment>
    </InfoCard>
    <InfoCard label="Contact" icon="email">
      <a href="mailto:chariri@chariri.moe">chariri@chariri.moe</a>
    </InfoCard>
    <InfoCard label="Postal Address" icon="mail">
      P.O. Box 21004294, Nanjing, Jiangsu 210042, P.R. China
    </InfoCard>
  </Cards>

  <SectionCluster icon="gear" title="Gear">
    <Cards columns="2">
      <InfoCard label="Rig" icon="radio">
        Wouxun KG-UV9D (Plus)
        <Fragment slot="description">FM @ VHF (144 MHz), 5 W</Fragment>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard label="Rig" icon="radio">
        ICOM IC-7300
        <Fragment slot="description">SSB, FT8 @ HF, 15 W</Fragment>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard label="Antenna" icon="antenna">
        DIAMOND SRH771
        <Fragment slot="description">Already a bit bent, but still somewhat usable.</Fragment>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard label="Antenna" icon="antenna"
        >HF portable inverted-V SWA antenna by BG8GVJ</InfoCard
      >
    </Cards>
  </SectionCluster>

  <SectionCluster icon="policy" title="QSL Policy">
    <Prose>
      <p>For each contact, I will send a paper card when any of the following applies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>we agreed during the QSO how the cards would be exchanged;</li>
        <li>
          the other station's mailing address can be easily found on QRZ.com or elsewhere, and the
          contact was neither a contest QSO nor an FT8 QSO;
        </li>
        <li>I receive a card from the other station first;</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In other cases, I will only upload the log to this site, LoTW, and QRZ.com. You can still
        contact me through the email or mailing address above if you want a card. When sending me a
        card or letter, no SASE is needed. For OMs with frequent contacts, I may combine several
        QSOs into one outgoing card, or omit some of them.
      </p>
      <p>
        I <strong>do not</strong> exchange eyeball QSL cards unless we have actually met offline.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </SectionCluster>
</SectionBlock>

<SectionBlock id="showcase" title="Showcase">
  <SectionCluster title="QSL Card" icon="gallery">
    <Cards columns="2">
      <GalleryCard
        src="/images/qsl/QSLCard.webp"
        alt="QSL card front with blanks for the contacted station's callsign and QSL confirmation type, plus a table for printing date, frequency, mode, signal report, power, and remarks."
        title="QSL v2 - Front"
      >
        This version is based on the <a href="https://forum.hamcq.cn/d/418">design</a> by <a
          href="https://shiro.love/"
        >
          Shiro
        </a> aka BI3AR, and was adjusted for printed filling instead of handwriting.
      </GalleryCard>
      <GalleryCard
        src="/images/qsl/QSLCard-Back.webp"
        alt="QSL card back showing the Chinese VOCALOID character Luo Tianyi operating a wall of amateur radio equipment, with a large BD4WXB callsign sign beside her."
        title="QSL v2 - Back"
      >
        The back <a href="https://t.bilibili.com/1054583074411511815">illustration</a> was drawn by
        <a href="https://space.bilibili.com/524445763">乐韵Jewel</a>.
      </GalleryCard>
      <GalleryCard
        src="/images/qsl/QSLCard-v1.webp"
        alt="First-edition QSL card front with handwritten fields for callsign, QSL confirmation type, date, time, mode, frequency, signal report, rig, power, and antenna."
        title="QSL v1 - Front"
      >
        The <a href="https://forum.hamcq.cn/d/418">design</a> is by <a href="https://shiro.love/">
          Shiro
        </a> aka BI3AR.
      </GalleryCard>
      <GalleryCard
        src="/images/qsl/QSLCard-Back-v1.webp"
        alt="First-edition QSL card back with a Luo Tianyi illustration, with BD4WXB and the name 茶栗chariri printed at the upper left."
        title="QSL v1 - Back"
      >
        The back illustration is <a href="https://www.pixiv.net/artworks/99486679">「🍀」</a> by artist
        <a href="https://www.pixiv.net/users/418969">TID</a>.
      </GalleryCard>
    </Cards>
  </SectionCluster>

  <SectionCluster title="Awards" icon="award">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <GalleryCard
        src="/images/award/202505zjvhf.avif"
        alt="Award certificate for the 2025 May 5 Zhejiang Province VHF DX Contest, with a Zhejiang Province map in the background, the ZARA logo at top left, BD4WXB ranked 6th with a score of 251, and serial number ZARA-VHF-1008 at bottom right."
        title="2025 May 5 Zhejiang VHF DX Contest"
      >
        <p>May 5, 2025 Zhejiang Amateur Radio Association Zhejiang Province VHF DX Contest</p>
        <p><strong>Rank</strong>: 6th</p>
        <p><strong>Score</strong>: 251</p>
      </GalleryCard>
    </div>
  </SectionCluster>
</SectionBlock>

<SectionBlock id="logbook" title="Logbook">
  <LogbookCard lang="en" callsign={profile.callsign} />
</SectionBlock>
